{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004",
  "title": "Charts with Plot",
  "created_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "shared_cargo_toml": "[profile.release]\nopt-level = 1\nlto = false\ncodegen-units = 16",
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "cell_0",
      "order": 0,
      "label": "Introduction",
      "cell_type": "Markdown",
      "source": "> *AI authored to showcase ironpad capabilities.*\n\n# Charts with `Plot` 📊\n\nironpad includes a built-in `Plot` helper that makes it easy to create charts. Under the hood it uses the **plotters** crate, but you don't need to set up backends or boilerplate — just call `Plot::line`, `Plot::bar`, or `Plot::scatter`.\n\nAll charts render as SVG with a dark theme that matches ironpad's UI.",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_1",
      "order": 1,
      "label": "Line Chart",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "// Generate some data: y = sin(x)\nlet data: Vec<(f64, f64)> = (0..=100)\n    .map(|i| {\n        let x = i as f64 * 0.1;\n        (x, x.sin())\n    })\n    .collect();\n\nPlot::line(&data)\n    .title(\"Sine Wave\")\n    .x_label(\"x\")\n    .y_label(\"sin(x)\")\n",
      "cargo_toml": null,
      "collapsed": true,
